Hi Murray,

Thanks for the very prompt response. Sorry if this is very naïve of me, but how do you incorporate the sampling intervals in your data? I haven’t found any examples of code in any of the tutorials I have.

This code tells me intervals is an unused argument

BL<-read.capthist(captfile="2016_2019AUG_BL_SECR_capturedata.txt",

                  trapfile = list("2016_BL_SECR_traplocs.txt",

                                  "2017_BL_SECR_traplocs.txt",

                                  "2018_BL_SECR_traplocs.txt",

                                  "2019MAY_BL_SECR_traplocs.txt",

                                  "2019AUG_BL_SECR_traplocs.txt"),

                  detector = "multi",

                  fmt=c("trapID","XY"),

                  covnames=list("Sex","Generation"),

                  intervals=c(12,12,12,3))

summary(BL)

The best info I’ve found so far is to sneak intervals in as a separate line.

intervals(OVpossumCH) <-c(123,91,154,118,85)/365# annual

Fit three models, two with season as a covariate. Intervals were not included in the secr dataset, so we sneak them in here. Sexes and ages are pooled

Thanks,

Cheryl

