'sneaking them in' is quite legit. As 'secr' itself had no use for intervals there was never an intervals argument to the read.capthist function. Intervals are covered briefly in Section 4 of the openCR vignette, and as an attribute of a capthist object in 'secr' (?intervals should work, but there is a naming conflict with a function in nlme) and in the examples vignette as you found. Note the use of zero interval between secondary sessions within a primary session. I agree the documentation could be improved...

